{%- set retired = ["Superseded", "Rejected"] -%}
{%- set vocab = vocabulary("lines") -%}
{%- set acc = namespace(rows=[], unused=[]) -%}
{%- for t in docs("THEORY", in_force=True) -%}
  {%- set r = namespace(lines=[], users=[]) -%}
  {%- for x in t.supports + t.corroborates + t.answers + t.bears_on + t.reports -%}
    {%- set d = x if x.code is defined else doc(x) -%}
    {%- if d.status not in retired and d.code not in r.users -%}
      {%- set r.users = r.users + [d.code] -%}
      {%- set l = d.line if d.line is not string else [d.line] -%}
      {%- if l and l[0] not in r.lines -%}{%- set r.lines = r.lines + [l[0]] -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- if r.lines -%}
    {%- set acc.rows = acc.rows + [{"t": t, "lines": r.lines, "users": r.users}] -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- set acc.unused = acc.unused + [t] -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
# Readings by line

*Which lines of the record's argument each reading in force serves, and
which readings no line yet builds on. Generated from `record/theory.d/` and
the entries that cite it: edit those, not this page.*

A reading (THEORY) is the record's account of what a work holds. It
carries no `line` of its own. A reading serves a line when an entry of that
line uses it: a claim or argument grounds on it, it corroborates a claim,
it answers or bears on a question, or it reports a case. Its lines are the
first lines of those entries, as ADR-085 reads a relation, and entries
that are Superseded or Rejected do not count. They are read off the
relations when this page is built, so a reading gains or loses a line as
the argument around it changes.

Of {{ acc.rows | length + acc.unused | length }} readings in force,
{{ acc.rows | length }} serve at least one line and {{ acc.unused | length }}
serve none.

